{
  "rationale": "The site moved from a table and definition-list layout to utility-class cards, so every selector had to be rebuilt by structure. Listing: each card is a direct child of div.grid, the follow link is the anchor in its h3, and the next-page link has aria-label 'Next page'. Detail page: the title is the h2. Category and location come from the first meta line ('Category · Location'). Reference, published date and status come from the meta line under the h2 ('Ref. X · Published D · Status: S'). The deadline is in the strong tag inside the slate box. The value is in the 'Estimated value:' paragraph; capturing its full remainder means 'Not disclosed' still maps to null. The authority is the font-semibold div in the border-t block. The description is the paragraph in the plain mt-6 div. Old label and regex strategies are kept as fallbacks.",
  "confidence": 0.8,
  "container": {
    "css": "div.grid > div.border"
  },
  "follow": {
    "css": "h3 a::attr(href)"
  },
  "next_page": {
    "css": "a[aria-label='Next page']::attr(href)"
  },
  "fields": [
